#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186305007 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083323 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01100ea8-2ab9-511e-8321-6ef5588c4417" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations to Compute an Unknown Mean or Standard Deviation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40a8a690-0e17-513a-9759-e2c32710072c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302862}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40a8a690-0e17-513a-9759-e2c32710072c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302862} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1c1b1da-a3d8-5b1d-9536-eeb4e916f1d1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304605}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cbfb0339-7153-551d-aafb-c429f4a2a68d" :question/math-academy-id "q-332239" :question/problem "A data set contains the observations ${x}_{1}=3.08,{x}_{2}=8.68$ with $z$-scores ${z}_{1}=-1.2$ and ${z}_{2}=2.3,$ respectively. Find the mean $\\overset{¯}{x}$ of the data set.\n\n$\\overset{¯}{x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nFrom the first observation, we have\n\n$$\n3.08=\\overset{¯}{x}+(-1.2)\\cdot \\sigma .\n$$\n\nFrom the second observation, we have\n\n$$\n8.68=\\overset{¯}{x}+2.3\\cdot \\sigma .\n$$\n\nSubtracting the first equation from the second and solving for $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8.68-3.08 & =(2.3-(-1.2))\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 5.6 & =3.5\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ \\sigma  & =1.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this value back into our first equation and solving for $\\overset{¯}{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3.08 & =\\overset{¯}{x}+(-1.2)\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 3.08 & =\\overset{¯}{x}+(-1.2)\\cdot 1.6 \\\\ 3.08 & =\\overset{¯}{x}-1.92 \\\\ \\overset{¯}{x} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
